 '[{"text":"Natural selection","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Use and disuse of organs","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Inheritance of acquired characteristics","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Random mutation alone, without selection","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Darwin proposed that natural selection -- the differential survival and reproduction of individuals with favorable heritable traits -- is the primary driver of evolution.'),
('NEET UG', 'Zoology', 'Genetics and Evolution', 'hard', 'mcq',
 'Homologous organs are organs that have:',
 '[{"text":"Similar structure and origin, indicating common ancestry, though they may serve different functions","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Similar function but different structure and origin","isCorrect":false},{"text":"No evolutionary significance at all","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Identical function and structure in unrelated species","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Homologous organs share a similar underlying structure and evolutionary origin (from a common ancestor), even if they have since evolved to perform different functions, such as a bird''s wing and a human arm.'),

-- Zoology: Biotechnology and its Applications
('NEET UG', 'Zoology', 'Biotechnology and its Applications', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Recombinant DNA technology primarily involves:',
 '[{"text":"Combining DNA from different sources to create new genetic combinations","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Destroying DNA in bacteria","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Sequencing an entire genome without modification","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Removing all genes from an organism","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Recombinant DNA technology involves combining DNA segments from different sources (often using restriction enzymes and ligases) to create novel genetic combinations.'),
('NEET UG', 'Zoology', 'Biotechnology and its Applications', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Human insulin used to treat diabetes is commercially manufactured using:',
 '[{"text":"Extraction directly from human pancreases only","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Genetically modified bacteria (such as E. coli)","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Chemical synthesis from plant extracts","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Extraction from animal blood only","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Human insulin is produced industrially by inserting the human insulin gene into bacteria (like E. coli), which then express and produce the insulin protein.'),
('NEET UG', 'Zoology', 'Biotechnology and its Applications', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Gel electrophoresis is a technique primarily used to:',
 '[{"text":"Amplify DNA fragments","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Separate DNA fragments based on their size","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Sequence proteins","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Destroy bacterial cells","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Gel electrophoresis separates DNA (or protein) fragments by size as they migrate through a gel matrix under an electric field, smaller fragments moving faster.'),
('NEET UG', 'Zoology', 'Biotechnology and its Applications', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Golden rice is a genetically modified crop that has been enriched with a precursor of which vitamin?',
 '[{"text":"Vitamin A (beta-carotene)","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Vitamin C","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Vitamin D","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Vitamin B12","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Golden rice is genetically engineered to produce beta-carotene, a precursor of Vitamin A, addressing Vitamin A deficiency in populations reliant on rice as a staple food.');
